# Natural Language Router

> When a message describes a problem in plain English (no slash command), automatically
> classify it using the map below and run the correct workflow WITHOUT asking for clarification.
> Diagnose first. If the diagnosis reveals the wrong path, adjust — do not ask upfront.

---

## SYMPTOM → WORKFLOW MAP

### LOGIN / ACCOUNT PROBLEMS
Trigger words: "can't log in", "login broken", "sign in not working", "keeps logging me out",
"logged out", "session expired", "kicked out", "redirect loop", "sends me back to login",
"Google login", "social login", "OAuth", "signup broken", "can't create account",
"register not working", "forgot password", "reset password", "blank after login",
"logged in but can't see anything", "dashboard blank after signing in"

→ Route to: `/fix-auth`

---

### DATA NOT LOADING / EMPTY STATE
Trigger words: "nothing is loading", "nothing shows up", "page is blank", "dashboard empty",
"data not showing", "can't see my data", "blank page", "empty list", "no results",
"nothing appears", "content missing", "records gone", "table empty",
"data was there now it's gone", "my items disappeared"

→ Check project type first:
  - If `src/contexts/AuthContext.tsx` exists OR data fetching is in hooks/useEffect → `/fix-data-sync`
  - Otherwise → `/fix-database`

---

